ar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron","html_url":"https://github.com/Amegatron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T17:13:42Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T17:13:42Z","body":"I would say this is still completely non-obvious and non-intuitive. First, this behaviour does not directly follow from the documentation. Like, the front of the car is +Z... Ok, but it does not say a lot. Secondly, and most importantly, this behavior is still weird even if you know about it. What I mean is that wheels are still capable to tract the vehicle in any direction. Why do they only rotate along the Z axis of the car itself? And not relative to theselves. Moreover, it really makes no sense if the wheel is moving orthogonally, but it still rotates, because it is in fact moving along the Z axis of the car.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137192174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137226327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109062#issuecomment-3137226327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109062","id":3137226327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66_kZX","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T17:25:44Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T17:25:44Z","body":"A bit of a clarification could help indeed, but I'd say it saying that +Z is the forward direction means exactly that, but if you have some good suggestions for how to improve the documentation to clarify that it would be very welcome!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137226327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137308823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109062#issuecomment-3137308823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109062","id":3137308823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66_4iX","user":{"login":"Amegatron","id":6664497,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6664497?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron","html_url":"https://github.com/Amegatron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T17:49:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T17:49:57Z","body":"Well, I think directly stating that wheels must be facing towards Z+ of the VehicleBody3D would do the job. But to me it still looks like a malfunctioning of the wheel, and they should rotate according to where exactly they are facing, either it is +X or whatever. I don't really know how exactly they are implemented internally, and perhaps that would require an overhaul. But at least they'll become true wheels :)\n\n> +Z is the forward direction means exactly that\n\nAs for this phrase I would like to clarify that it makes things kinda clear only for ordinary cars like IRL which just move forward/backward. But since in game-dev we can come up with any kinds of moving vehicles, this is no longer obvious, because these wheels are interpreted more arbitrarily, like it's truly a wheel-tractor of you vehicle which could push the \"car\" in any direction. And it truly can now. But the rotation is still bound to only +Z direction of the car for some reason.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137308823/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137314332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109062#issuecomment-3137314332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109062","id":3137314332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66_54c","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T17:52:08Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T17:52:08Z","body":"But the VehicleBody class is very minimal and not intended for more advanced or strange cases","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137314332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"per