os/godotengine/godot/issues/109062","id":3137394540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67ANds","user":{"login":"Amegatron","id":6664497,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6664497?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron","html_url":"https://github.com/Amegatron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Amegatron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T18:21:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T18:22:14Z","body":"Yeah. I got your point. I'm still saying there is an issue tho. Either the Vehicle is meant to be that simple to represent a real-world car and necessarily has to have \"front\". Or it can be just an abstract vehicle without any direction. In first case, if this is by design, the wheels should be locked to facing only Z+, in other words - any rotation of them in the editor having no effect. Or, in the latter case, the wheels should depict the real rotation, corresponding to where they are facing in fact, making them a more versatile physical/mechanical component.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3137394540/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]